          "id": "item_1",
          "type": "agent_message",
          "text": "- **High — Probe cleanup can falsely settle an uncertain Docker create.**  \n  **Evidence:** `packages/workflow-control/src/developmentHost.ts` — `#probe`, `#removeProbe`, `#reconcileProbes`; `packages/workflow-control/src/developmentHostJournal.ts` — `reconcileDevelopmentProbe`.  \n  **Reason:** If probe creation times out, `#removeProbe` treats an absent inspection result as confirmed cancellation. Reconciliation can then delete the token directory and mark the probe settled, although a previously submitted Docker create may still complete. This loses the pending cleanup obligation across restart. The worker launcher correctly preserves this uncertainty; the probe path does not.  \n  **Proposed correction:** Persist probe create-dispatch and acknowledgement state. Preserve pending cleanup after an initiated, uncertain create until settlement is established; absence alone must not confirm cancellation.  \n  **Missing evidence:** A delayed probe-create completion after timeout and initially absent inspection, including supervisor restart. Assert that cleanup remains pending and any late container is reconciled before readiness.\n\nThe supplied guarded-create helper and both rejection regressions address review15’s finding. Retained logs report the stated passing suites and current-image generation/revocation check. The probe finding prevents a “no remaining actionable blockers” conclusion.\n\nEvidence-only review; no commands executed or state changed. This is not human or merge approval."
        }
